<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gurgen I of Lori</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. c. 979–989</span> · Also known as Kiurike I</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gurgen, also known as Kiurike I, was the son of King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ashot-iii-of-armenia">Ashot III of Bagratid Armenia</a> and founder of the Kingdom of Lori, also called Tashir-Dzoraget, in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/armenia">Armenia</a>. Around 979 he received the northern provinces and took the title of king, founding the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kiurikian-dynasty">Kiurikian dynasty</a>. The kingdom's monasteries of Haghpat and Sanahin flourished under his line.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gurgen-i-of-lori.jpg" alt="Gurgen I of Lori" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Yerevantsi · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Haghpat_monastery_bas_relief.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
